WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.261 --> 00:00:05.121
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:05.121 --> 00:00:08.288
(inspirational music)

00:00:42.825 --> 00:00:45.090
(upbeat music)

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:47.440
- [Narrator] Long considered
the caviar of the East,

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.280
bird's nests, or, more
specifically, the dried saliva

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.090
of swiftlet birds is a rare treat.

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:55.950
These birds prefer to build
their nests in dark caves,

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:58.040
and on Nabat Island in the Philippines,

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:00.920
nest-gatherers go to
great heights, literally,

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:01.753
to collect them.

00:01:02.786 --> 00:01:06.703
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:44.444 --> 00:01:46.750
The work may be dangerous,
but these nest-gatherers

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:48.720
are willing to risk their lives because

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:50.746
the payoff is worth it.

00:01:50.746 --> 00:01:54.645
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:54.645 --> 00:01:57.562
(thoughtful music)

00:02:12.919 --> 00:02:14.750
Traditionally, the role of a nest-gatherer

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:17.710
is passed down from
generation to generation,

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:19.470
so while this may seem frightening,

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:21.870
for Angelito, it's an honor.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:25.787
(speaking in foreign language)

